cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or research findings in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "XRL-IDARS: Explainable Reinforcement Learning Intrusion Detection and Autonomous Response System"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-05
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rishikeshgowdakk/fyp-xrlids"
authors:
  - family-names: "Gowda K K"
    given-names: "Rishikesh"
abstract: >-
  XRL-IDARS is an open-source research framework for network-flow intrusion detection and
  controlled autonomous response. It couples tabular and temporal machine learning detection
  (Random Forest and LSTM score fusion) with TreeSHAP feature attributions, context-aware
  reinforcement learning response policies (Dueling DQN), and deterministic safety constraints
  with atomic transaction rollback to prevent self-inflicted denial-of-service and unauthorized
  network mutations.
keywords:
  - intrusion-detection
  - network-security
  - reinforcement-learning
  - dueling-dqn
  - explainable-ai
  - shap
  - cybersecurity
